# Dockerignore for the API image.
#
# The context is the repository root (the build needs the workspace manifests), so
# without this the daemon ships node_modules, dist, .env and the database backups to
# the builder — gigabytes, several minutes per build, and a .env in an image layer.

# Secrets. .env holds DATABASE_URL and MSG91_AUTH_KEY. Baking it into an image puts
# it in a layer that survives history rewrites short of a rebuild from scratch.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build

# Database dumps. A backup in an image is a data leak in an image.
api/backups

.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# app/ and web/ source is NOT excluded, despite the API image not needing it.
#
# npm workspaces will not install without every workspace manifest present, so the
# Dockerfile copies app/package.json and web/package.json before `npm ci`. Excluding
# those directories here breaks the build at COPY time — which is what happened the
# first time this was written. Their node_modules is covered by **/node_modules above.
scripts
*.md
*.log
*.dump

.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db